---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import map from '../generated/model-map.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const n = map.models.length;
const p = map.projections;
const pct = (x) => Math.round(x * 100);
---

<BaseLayout title="Map | Model Personality Browser" description="Every model in the corpus placed by how its freeflow prose resembles every other model's — a rotatable 3D map, a dendrogram, and lab trajectories over time.">
  <div class="map-page">
  <h1>Model map</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every model in the corpus, placed by how its freeflow prose resembles every other model's. Distance here is <em>style</em>, not capability:
    the character n-gram centroid of each model's freeflow samples, compared pairwise by cosine, then projected down to something you can rotate.
  </p>

  <section class="map-shell">
    <aside class="rail">
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Projection</legend>
        <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Dimensions">
          <button id="dim3" aria-pressed="true">3D</button><button id="dim2" aria-pressed="false">2D</button>
        </div>
        <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Method">
          <button id="mUmap" aria-pressed="true">UMAP</button><button id="mMds" aria-pressed="false">MDS</button><button id="mPca" aria-pressed="false">PCA</button>
        </div>
        <p class="keep" id="keep"></p>
      </fieldset>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Overlay</legend>
        <label class="row"><span>Link each model to its <b id="kv">3</b> nearest</span><input id="k" type="range" min="0" max="6" value="3" /></label>
        <label class="row check"><input id="traj" type="checkbox" /><span>Lab trajectories (release order)</span></label>
      </fieldset>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Time</legend>
        <label class="row"><span>Released up to <b id="datev"></b></span></label>
        <input id="date" type="range" min="0" max="1000" value="1000" aria-label="Release date cut-off" style="width:100%" />
      </fieldset>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Find</legend>
        <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="model or strapline…" aria-label="Find a model" />
      </fieldset>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Labs</legend>
        <div class="labs" id="labs"></div>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="card" id="card"><div class="lab">Hover or search</div><h2>—</h2><p class="strap">Nearest neighbours in the full space appear here.</p></div>
    </aside>
    <div id="plot" role="img" aria-label="Scatter plot of models by prose similarity"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="dendro-shell">
    <h2>Family tree</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The same distances, without the squash: average-linkage hierarchical clustering over the full cosine matrix. Branch length is distance; nothing is lost to projection.
      Leaves are coloured by lab, so you can see where the tree recovers labs on its own — and where it doesn't.
    </p>
    <div class="dendro-wrap"><svg id="dendro" aria-label="Dendrogram of models"></svg></div>
  </section>

  <section class="method">
    <h2>Method and honesty</h2>
    <p>
      For each of the {n} models, the {map.generated_from.freeflow_docs.toLocaleString()} freeflow samples are vectorised as character 3–5-gram TF-IDF and averaged into one centroid per model.
      Cosine similarity between centroids gives a {n}×{n} matrix; that matrix is the ground truth for everything on this page.
      The map projects it into two or three axes and necessarily loses structure. The number beside each projection is how much of it survives:
      for each model, the share of its three nearest neighbours in the full space that are still among its three nearest on the map.
    </p>
    <ul class="metrics">
      <li><b>UMAP</b> 2D {pct(p.umap2.knn3)}% · 3D {pct(p.umap3.knn3)}% — best neighbourhoods, but the gaps between clusters are an artefact</li>
      <li><b>MDS</b> 2D {pct(p.mds2.knn3)}% · 3D {pct(p.mds3.knn3)}% — honest global distances, blurrier locally</li>
      <li><b>PCA</b> 2D {pct(p.pca2.knn3)}% · 3D {pct(p.pca3.knn3)}% — linear; explains {pct(p.pca2.variance)}% / {pct(p.pca3.variance)}% of variance</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      So read the <em>drawn edges</em> (true nearest neighbours) and the <em>tree</em> as the claim, and the positions as the sketch.
      Two known facts to calibrate by: Ox Alpha, later confirmed as GLM-5.3-Flash, sits at 0.96 to it; the two Ox Alpha snapshots sit at 0.97 to each other.
      Same-lab models cluster because of shared post-training; models that distil from a lab cluster with it too, so proximity is a fact about training, not about quality.
      Stealth models are ringed. Data: <a href={base}>this corpus</a>; generator: <code>website/scripts/generate_map.py</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/plotly.js/2.31.1/plotly.min.js"></script>
<script is:inline src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/d3/7.9.0/d3.min.js"></script>
<script is:inline define:vars={{ map, base }}>
  const M = map.models, N = M.length, SIM = map.sim, ORDER = map.order;
  const idxOf = Object.fromEntries(ORDER.map((m, i) => [m, i]));
  const PAL = ['#b5442a','#245d68','#3f7d4e','#7b4fa8','#b7791a','#1f8a99','#a83a78','#6b7f35','#8a5a3c','#4c5ea0'];
  const labCounts = {}; M.forEach(m => { labCounts[m.lab] = (labCounts[m.lab] || 0) + 1; });
  const labs = Object.keys(labCounts).sort((a, b) => labCounts[b] - labCounts[a]);
  const TOP = labs.filter(l => l !== 'Unknown').slice(0, PAL.length);
  const color = l => { const i = TOP.indexOf(l); return i >= 0 ? PAL[i] : '#8f8b82'; };
  const hexRgb = h => [1, 3, 5].map(k => parseInt(h.slice(k, k + 2), 16));
  const tint = (h, f) => { const [r, g, b] = hexRgb(h); const m = c => Math.round(c + (255 - c) * f); return `rgb(${m(r)},${m(g)},${m(b)})`; }; // f=0 full colour, f=1 white
  const dates = M.map(m => m.date ? Date.parse(m.date) : NaN).filter(x => !isNaN(x));
  const dMin = Math.min(...dates), dMax = Math.max(...dates);
  const state = { dims: 3, method: 'umap', k: 3, hidden: new Set(), q: '', focus: null, traj: false, cut: dMax };
  const NN = M.map(m => m.nn.map(([name, s]) => [s, idxOf[name]]));
  const coords = i => M[i].coords[state.method + state.dims];
  const visible = i => !state.hidden.has(M[i].lab) && !(M[i].date && Date.parse(M[i].date) > state.cut);
  const matches = i => { if (!state.q) return false; const q = state.q.toLowerCase(), m = M[i]; return m.model.includes(q) || m.display.toLowerCase().includes(q) || (m.strapline || '').toLowerCase().includes(q); };
  const esc = s => String(s || '').replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;');
  const css = v => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(v).trim();

  function build() {
    const ink = css('--ink'), muted = css('--muted'), paper = css('--paper-strong'), line = css('--line');
    const traces = [];
    const three = state.dims === 3;
    if (state.k > 0) {
      const ex = [], ey = [], ez = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { if (!visible(i)) continue;
        for (const [, j] of NN[i].slice(0, state.k)) { if (!visible(j)) continue; if (j < i && NN[j].slice(0, state.k).some(x => x[1] === i)) continue;
          const a = coords(i), b = coords(j); ex.push(a[0], b[0], null); ey.push(a[1], b[1], null); if (three) ez.push(a[2], b[2], null); } }
      traces.push(Object.assign({ x: ex, y: ey, mode: 'lines', hoverinfo: 'skip', showlegend: false, line: { color: 'rgba(38,37,33,0.22)', width: 2 }, name: 'edges' }, three ? { type: 'scatter3d', z: ez } : { type: 'scattergl' }));
    }
    if (state.traj) {
      for (const lab of labs) { if (state.hidden.has(lab)) continue;
        const idx = M.map((m, i) => i).filter(i => M[i].lab === lab && visible(i) && M[i].date).sort((a, b) => Date.parse(M[a].date) - Date.parse(M[b].date));
        if (idx.length < 2) continue;
        const base = color(lab), n = idx.length;
        const shade = k => tint(base, 0.75 * (1 - k / (n - 1)));   // first release pale, latest full colour
        if (three) {
          traces.push({ type: 'scatter3d', mode: 'lines', hoverinfo: 'skip', showlegend: false, legendgroup: lab, name: lab + ' path',
            x: idx.map(i => coords(i)[0]), y: idx.map(i => coords(i)[1]), z: idx.map(i => coords(i)[2]),
            line: { width: 6, color: idx.map((_, k) => k), colorscale: [[0, tint(base, 0.75)], [1, base]], cmin: 0, cmax: n - 1 }, opacity: 0.85 });
        } else {
          for (let k = 0; k < n - 1; k++) { const a = coords(idx[k]), b = coords(idx[k + 1]);
            traces.push({ type: 'scattergl', mode: 'lines', hoverinfo: 'skip', showlegend: false, legendgroup: lab, x: [a[0], b[0]], y: [a[1], b[1]], line: { width: 4, color: shade(k + 1) }, opacity: 0.85 }); }
        }
      }
    }
    for (const lab of labs) {
      if (state.hidden.has(lab)) { traces.push(Object.assign({ name: `${lab} (${labCounts[lab]})`, legendgroup: lab, mode: 'markers', visible: 'legendonly', x: [null], y: [null], marker: { color: color(lab) }, hoverinfo: 'skip' }, three ? { type: 'scatter3d', z: [null] } : { type: 'scattergl' })); continue; }
      const idx = []; for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) if (M[i].lab === lab && visible(i)) idx.push(i); if (!idx.length) continue;
      const isUnk = lab === 'Unknown';
      const t = { name: `${lab} (${labCounts[lab]})`, legendgroup: lab, mode: 'markers', customdata: idx, hovertemplate: '%{text}<extra></extra>',
        text: idx.map(i => `<b>${esc(M[i].display)}</b><br><span style="font-size:11px">${esc(M[i].lab)} · ${esc(M[i].date || '')}</span><br><i>${esc(M[i].strapline)}</i>`),
        marker: { size: idx.map(i => matches(i) || state.focus === i ? (three ? 12 : 18) : (three ? 7 : 10)), color: color(lab), opacity: 0.95,
          line: { width: idx.map(i => isUnk || matches(i) || state.focus === i ? 2 : 0.5), color: idx.map(i => matches(i) || state.focus === i ? ink : (isUnk ? css('--amber') : paper)) } },
        x: idx.map(i => coords(i)[0]), y: idx.map(i => coords(i)[1]) };
      if (three) { t.type = 'scatter3d'; t.z = idx.map(i => coords(i)[2]); } else t.type = 'scattergl';
      traces.push(t);
    }
    // Fixed axis ranges over ALL models for this projection, so hiding labs or scrubbing time never rescales the scene.
    const key = state.method + state.dims;
    const ext = [0, 1, 2].slice(0, state.dims).map(a => { let lo = Infinity, hi = -Infinity; for (const m of M) { const v = m.coords[key][a]; if (v < lo) lo = v; if (v > hi) hi = v; } const pad = (hi - lo) * 0.06; return [lo - pad, hi + pad]; });
    const ax = { showgrid: true, gridcolor: line, zeroline: false, showticklabels: false, title: '', backgroundcolor: paper, showspikes: false, autorange: false };
    const layout = { paper_bgcolor: paper, plot_bgcolor: paper, font: { family: 'Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif', color: muted, size: 12 }, margin: { l: 8, r: 8, t: 8, b: 8 },
      legend: { orientation: 'h', y: -0.02, x: 0, font: { size: 11, color: muted }, bgcolor: 'rgba(0,0,0,0)', itemsizing: 'constant' },
      hoverlabel: { bgcolor: paper, bordercolor: line, font: { color: ink, size: 12, family: 'Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif' } },
      // uirevision keeps the user's camera / pan / zoom across every update; it changes only when the projection changes (a real reset).
      uirevision: key,
      scene: { uirevision: key, xaxis: Object.assign({}, ax, { range: ext[0] }), yaxis: Object.assign({}, ax, { range: ext[1] }), zaxis: Object.assign({}, ax, { range: three ? ext[2] : undefined }),
        bgcolor: paper, camera: { eye: { x: 0.95, y: 0.85, z: 0.6 } }, aspectmode: 'cube', dragmode: 'orbit' },
      xaxis: Object.assign({}, ax, { range: ext[0], uirevision: key }), yaxis: Object.assign({}, ax, { range: ext[1], uirevision: key }), dragmode: three ? 'orbit' : 'pan' };
    Plotly.react('plot', traces, layout, { responsive: true, displaylogo: false, modeBarButtonsToRemove: ['select2d', 'lasso2d', 'toImage'] });
    const plot = document.getElementById('plot');
    if (!plot.__wired) { plot.__wired = true;
      plot.on('plotly_hover', ev => { const p = ev.points[0]; if (p && p.customdata != null) showCard(p.customdata); });
      plot.on('plotly_legendclick', ev => { const lab = ev.data[ev.curveNumber].legendgroup; if (!lab) return true;
        state.hidden.has(lab) ? state.hidden.delete(lab) : state.hidden.add(lab);
        const cb = document.querySelector(`.labs input[data-lab="${CSS.escape(lab)}"]`); if (cb) cb.checked = !state.hidden.has(lab);
        build(); return false; });
      plot.on('plotly_legenddoubleclick', () => false);
      plot.on('plotly_click', ev => { const p = ev.points[0]; if (p && p.customdata != null) { state.focus = p.customdata; showCard(p.customdata); build(); highlightLeaf(p.customdata); } }); }
  }
  function showCard(i) { const m = M[i];
    document.getElementById('card').innerHTML = `<div class="lab">${esc(m.lab)} · ${esc(m.family)} · ${esc(m.date || '')}</div><h2><a href="${base}models/${m.model}/">${esc(m.display)}</a></h2><p class="strap">${esc(m.strapline) || '—'}</p><ol>${m.nn.slice(0, 3).map(([name, s]) => `<li><b>${esc(M[idxOf[name]].display)}</b> ${s.toFixed(3)}</li>`).join('')}</ol>`; }
  function keep() { const key = state.method + state.dims, pr = map.projections[key]; const extra = pr.variance != null ? `, ${Math.round(pr.variance * 100)}% of variance` : '';
    document.getElementById('keep').textContent = `Keeps ${Math.round(pr.knn3 * 100)}% of each model’s 3 nearest neighbours${extra}.`; }
  function press(id, on) { document.getElementById(id).setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false'); }
  function setDims(d) { state.dims = d; press('dim3', d === 3); press('dim2', d === 2); keep(); build(); }
  function setMethod(m) { state.method = m; press('mUmap', m === 'umap'); press('mMds', m === 'mds'); press('mPca', m === 'pca'); keep(); build(); }
  document.getElementById('dim3').onclick = () => setDims(3);
  document.getElementById('dim2').onclick = () => setDims(2);
  document.getElementById('mUmap').onclick = () => setMethod('umap');
  document.getElementById('mMds').onclick = () => setMethod('mds');
  document.getElementById('mPca').onclick = () => setMethod('pca');
  document.getElementById('k').oninput = e => { state.k = +e.target.value; document.getElementById('kv').textContent = state.k; build(); };
  document.getElementById('traj').onchange = e => { state.traj = e.target.checked; build(); };
  const dateEl = document.getElementById('date'), dateV = document.getElementById('datev');
  const fmt = t => new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  dateV.textContent = fmt(dMax);
  dateEl.oninput = e => { state.cut = dMin + (dMax - dMin) * (+e.target.value / 1000); dateV.textContent = fmt(state.cut); build(); };
  document.getElementById('q').oninput = e => { state.q = e.target.value.trim(); state.focus = null; build(); if (state.q) { const i = M.findIndex((_, i) => matches(i)); if (i >= 0) { showCard(i); highlightLeaf(i); } } };
  const labsEl = document.getElementById('labs');
  labsEl.innerHTML = labs.map(l => `<label><input type="checkbox" data-lab="${esc(l)}" checked><span class="sw" style="background:${color(l)}"></span>${esc(l)} <span class="n">${labCounts[l]}</span></label>`).join('');
  labsEl.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(cb => cb.addEventListener('change', () => { cb.checked ? state.hidden.delete(cb.dataset.lab) : state.hidden.add(cb.dataset.lab); build(); }));
  keep(); build();

  // ---- dendrogram ----
  const root = d3.hierarchy(map.tree, d => d.c);
  const leaves = root.leaves(); const rowH = 15, W = Math.min(1100, Math.max(700, document.querySelector('.dendro-wrap').clientWidth - 8)), labelW = 190, H = leaves.length * rowH + 20;
  const svg = d3.select('#dendro').attr('viewBox', `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr('width', '100%').attr('height', H);
  const cluster = d3.cluster().size([H - 20, W - labelW - 20]).separation(() => 1);
  cluster(root);
  const maxH = root.data.h || 1;
  const xOf = d => 10 + (W - labelW - 20) * (1 - (d.data.h || 0) / maxH);
  root.each(d => { d.y = xOf(d); });
  svg.append('g').selectAll('path').data(root.links()).join('path')
    .attr('fill', 'none').attr('stroke', css('--muted')).attr('stroke-opacity', 0.55).attr('stroke-width', 1.2)
    .attr('d', l => `M${l.source.y},${l.source.x + 10}V${l.target.x + 10}H${l.target.y}`);
  const leafG = svg.append('g').selectAll('g').data(leaves).join('g').attr('transform', d => `translate(${d.y},${d.x + 10})`).attr('class', 'leaf').attr('data-i', d => idxOf[d.data.m]);
  leafG.append('circle').attr('r', 3.5).attr('cx', 4).attr('fill', d => color(M[idxOf[d.data.m]].lab));
  leafG.append('text').attr('x', 11).attr('dy', '0.32em').attr('font-size', 11).attr('fill', css('--ink')).text(d => M[idxOf[d.data.m]].display);
  leafG.style('cursor', 'pointer').on('mouseenter', (_, d) => showCard(idxOf[d.data.m])).on('click', (_, d) => { state.focus = idxOf[d.data.m]; build(); showCard(state.focus); document.getElementById('plot').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' }); });
  function highlightLeaf(i) { leafG.select('text').attr('font-weight', d => idxOf[d.data.m] === i ? 700 : 400); }
</script>

<style is:global>
  .map-page .map-shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 240px 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 18px; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .map-page .map-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .map-page .rail { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; min-width: 0; }
  .map-page fieldset { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 12px 12px; margin: 0; background: var(--paper); min-width: 0; }
  .map-page legend { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); padding: 0 4px; }
  .map-page .seg { display: flex; gap: 4px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .map-page .seg button { background: var(--paper-strong); color: var(--muted); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 10px; font: inherit; font-size: 12.5px; cursor: pointer; }
  .map-page .seg button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
  .map-page .seg button:focus-visible, .map-page input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }
  .map-page .keep { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
  .map-page label.row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .map-page label.row.check { justify-content: flex-start; margin-top: 8px; }
  .map-page input[type="range"] { accent-color: var(--accent); width: 110px; }
  .map-page input[type="search"] { width: 100%; background: var(--paper-strong); color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 8px; font: inherit; font-size: 13px; }
  .map-page .labs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .map-page .labs label { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin: 0; cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); text-align: left; }
  .map-page .labs .n { color: var(--line-strong); }
  .map-page .labs input { accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .map-page .sw { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; flex: none; }
  .map-page .card { background: var(--paper-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 12px; min-height: 96px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .map-page .card h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 2px; }
  .map-page .card h2 a { text-decoration: none; }
  .map-page .card .lab { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .map-page .card .strap { font-style: italic; margin: 6px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  .map-page .card ol { margin: 6px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .map-page .card ol b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .map-page #plot { min-height: 560px; height: 72vh; background: var(--paper-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .map-page .dendro-shell { margin-top: 40px; }
  .map-page .dendro-wrap { background: var(--paper-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 8px; overflow-x: auto; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .map-page .method { margin-top: 40px; max-width: 78ch; }
  .map-page .metrics { padding-left: 20px; }
  .map-page .metrics li { margin: 4px 0; }
</style>
